(D5 - Discrepancy 5 repro: LANGUAGE.md:4516-4524 names no timezone for
 the time components. They are UTC - they match the UTC decomposition of
 `unix`, and they do not move when TZ does. Run this with TZ set to
 something an hour or more from UTC and it still says UTC:
   TZ=America/New_York ./p
 gave the same verdict on a machine whose local clock read 00:01 while the
 program's hour read 4.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D5.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the hour property is the UTC hour
)
Get current time into now.
a number called 'the utc hour' is now's unix modulo 86400 divide 3600.
If now's hour is 'the utc hour' then, print "the hour property is the UTC hour".
Otherwise, print "the hour property {now's hour} is not the UTC hour {'the utc hour'}".
